  <section id="problem">
    <h2 class="logo-heading"><span class="name-light">The</span> <span class="name-bold">problem</span></h2>
    <p>It can be hard for pet owners to know which food, accessories and medicine are best for their pet. Busy families and young pet owners often don’t have the time or knowledge to find out.</p>
    <p><strong>The goal:</strong> design a pet food and health app that lets people pick the best food for their pet quickly and easily.</p>
    <p class="case-meta">Responsibilities: conducting interviews, paper and digital wireframing, low- and high-fidelity prototyping, conducting usability studies, accounting for accessibility, and iterating on designs.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="research">
    <h2 class="logo-heading"><span class="name-light">Understanding</span> <span class="name-bold">the user</span></h2>
    <p>I conducted interviews and created empathy maps to understand who I was designing for. The main user group was working adults who don’t have time to research pet food or health and don’t know what’s best. Research also showed that people love the convenience of ordering from home, that many just pick the first food they see at the store, and that the sheer amount of pet food out there is overwhelming.</p>
    <div class="case-pains">
      <div><h3>Time</h3><p>Working adults are too busy to research the best food and health information for their pet.</p></div>
      <div><h3>User flow</h3><p>Some platforms make it really hard to set up a pet profile and use the app.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Options</h3><p>The amount of food and health information out there feels overwhelming.</p></div>
    </div>
